 "youtube": {
  "title": "Lighthouse of Alexandria: Where Did a Wonder Go?",
  "description": "The Lighthouse of Alexandria was one of the Seven Wonders of the Ancient World: three towers in one on the island of Pharos, possibly over 100 metres tall, its fire guiding ships into the harbour. Earthquakes cracked it again and again until only a stump was left, and in 1477 Sultan Qaitbay built a fortress on the spot from its stones. The rest is still down there: divers mapped its blocks and statues on the harbour floor in 1994.\n\nSubscribe to Stickstory for a true story like this every day. Which ancient wonder would you bring back? Tell us in the comments!\n\n#shorts #lighthouseofalexandria #stickstory",
